# Test: an AAA chain the daemon cannot BUILD falls over to the local accounts.
#
# OWNER RULING, 2026-09-04: "failover to local user if aaa fails MUST be the
# documented behaviour." This drives it through the daemon on the path that did
# the opposite until 058567f39.
#
# The config carries a bgp block ON PURPOSE. That selects the infraSetup boot
# path, which gated the whole ssh server on a non-nil AAA bundle: a keyless
# TACACS+ server made the build fail, the bundle stayed nil, and ssh was never
# started. The operator kept a forwarding router and lost every way into it.
#
# The tacacs server declares no key. RFC 8907 Section 10.5.2 requires a shared
# secret and forbids a client to set TAC_PLUS_UNENCRYPTED_FLAG, so
# tacacsBackend.Build refuses the server and the whole bundle build fails.
#
# VALIDATES: with the AAA chain unbuilt, ssh still starts and a LOCAL account
#            logs in.
# PREVENTS: a mistyped AAA block locking the operator out of a running daemon.
#           Without the fix the fixture cannot connect at all, because there is
#           no listener to connect to.
#
# THE LOGIN IS ALL THIS PROVES. Authorization is a separate answer and it is
# unchanged: a nil AAA bundle installs no policy, so liveAAABundleAuthorizer
# denies every command even though the login resolved the admin profile. The
# fixture reads that refusal to tell a successful login from a failed one, and
# `show bgp` is REFUSED here. An operator who reaches the box this way can log
# in and cannot yet act, which is recorded in
# plan/journal/guard-blocks-its-own-authors-repair.md.

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection { remote { ip 127.0.0.1; } local { ip 127.0.0.1; accept false; } }
		session { asn { local 65533; remote 65533; } }
	}
}
system {
	authentication {
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
			profile [ admin ]
		}
		tacacs {
			server 127.0.0.1 { port 49; }
			timeout 2
		}
	}
	authorization {
		profile admin { run { default-action allow; } edit { default-action allow; } }
	}
}
environment { ssh { enabled true; server main { ip 127.0.0.1; port $PORT2; } } }
EOF_CONF

# The daemon runs in the BACKGROUND and the fixture in the foreground. It cannot
# be an in-config observer that shuts the daemon down at the end: `request
# shutdown` travels the same dispatch path and the nil-bundle authorizer refuses
# it too, so the daemon would outlive the test and the run would time out.
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-conf
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/aaa-local-failover $PORT2:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
# The chain really did fail to build. Without this the test would also pass
# against a daemon whose TACACS+ config was simply ignored.
expect=stderr:pattern=no shared secret configured for this TACACS\+ server
expect=stderr:contains=AAA backend build failed
# And the operator still got in, on a local account.
expect=stderr:pattern=auth success.*source=local
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: local login succeeded with the AAA chain unbuilt
reject=stderr:pattern=source=tacacs
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
